§ `REQ-0288 (Haziq h080) -- the company as occupier, the agency as employer`

-- The company has charge, management or control of the tower it leases; the officer is at work on its stairwell. The agency
-- employs him; it does not control the tower. The company does not direct how he works. Engaged in March 2024.
-- s 11: the company, as occupier, must take reasonably practicable measures to make the workplace and its means of access safe
-- to everyone within -- including a person who is not its employee.
#ASSERT `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the software company` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol`

-- s 12(1): the company is not his employer, so it owes him no s 12(1) duty.
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 12(1) duty to the person as its employee` `the software company` `the security officer on patrol`

-- s 12(1): the agency is his employer, and he is at work, so it owes him the s 12(1) duty -- on premises it does not occupy.
#ASSERT `owes the section 12(1) duty to the person as its employee` `the security agency` `the security officer on patrol`

-- s 11: the agency is not the occupier, so it owes no s 11 duty for the stairwell.
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the security agency` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol`

-- s 10(c): neither duty is diminished by the other.
#ASSERT NOT `the duty is diminished because another also owes one` TRUE

-- s 14(1), (2): as the agency's principal, the company owes the officer the s 14(1) duty only if it directs how he works; here
-- it does not.
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 14(1) duty to the contractor's employee` `the software company` `the security officer on patrol`

-- s 14A(1): but it must take reasonable measures to ensure the agency (engaged after 1 September 2011) has the expertise and has
-- taken adequate safety measures.
#ASSERT `owes the section 14A duty about the contractor's expertise and measures` `the software company`

-- Heads of duty owed on these facts: the company two (ss 11, 14A); the agency one (s 12(1)).
#ASSERT `the number of duty heads owed` `the software company` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the number of duty heads owed` `the security agency` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol` EQUALS 1

-- s 20 with s 50(b): breach of either duty by a company -- fine up to $500,000, and $5,000 a day if it continues after conviction.
#ASSERT `the maximum fine` `breach of a Part 4 duty` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 500000
#ASSERT `the maximum daily fine after conviction` `breach of a Part 4 duty` TRUE EQUALS 5000

-- s 60(1): the Act gives the officer no civil action; s 59: it does not derogate from other written law (such as the Work Injury
-- Compensation Act 2019, which this Act does not otherwise address).
#ASSERT NOT `the Act itself gives a right to sue` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Act derogates from the other written law` "Work Injury Compensation Act 2019"

§ `4(1), 5(1) -- occupier and workplace`

#ASSERT `is the occupier of the workplace` `the software company` `the leased office tower`
#ASSERT NOT `is the occupier of the workplace` `the landlord without control` `the leased office tower`
#ASSERT NOT `is the occupier of the workplace` `the software company` `a registered factory`
#ASSERT `the premises are a workplace` `the leased office tower`
#ASSERT NOT `the premises are a workplace` `an empty unlet floor`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the software company` `an empty unlet floor` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol`

§ `11 -- whom and where the occupier's duty reaches`

#ASSERT `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the software company` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `a visitor to the tower`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the software company` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the officer off the premises`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the software company` `the leased office tower` `another tenant's corridor` `the security officer on patrol`
#ASSERT `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the software company` `the leased office tower` `the stairwell as strata common property` `the security officer on patrol`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 11 occupier's duty to the person for the spot` `the landlord without control` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol`

§ `19 -- the common area`

#ASSERT `the spot is a common area treated as part of the workplace` `the stairwell as strata common property`
#ASSERT NOT `the spot is a common area treated as part of the workplace` `common property nobody at work uses`
#ASSERT `owes the section 19 common-area duty for access and egress` `the management corporation` `the stairwell as strata common property`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 19 common-area duty for access and egress` `the landlord without control` `the stairwell as strata common property`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 19 common-area duty for access and egress` `the management corporation` `the wet stairwell`
#ASSERT `the number of duty heads owed` `the software company` `the leased office tower` `the stairwell as strata common property` `the security officer on patrol` EQUALS 3

§ `12(2), 14, 14A -- the company as employer and as principal`

#ASSERT `owes the section 14(1) duty to the contractor's employee` `the software company directing the guards` `the security officer on patrol`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 14(3) duty to the person` `the software company directing the guards` `the security officer on patrol`
#ASSERT `the number of duty heads owed` `the software company directing the guards` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `owes the section 12(2) duty to the person as a non-employee` `the software company whose cleaners mopped the stairs`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 12(2) duty to the person as a non-employee` `the security agency`
#ASSERT `owes the section 14(3) duty to the person` `the software company whose cleaners mopped the stairs` `the security officer on patrol`
#ASSERT `the number of duty heads owed` `the software company whose cleaners mopped the stairs` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 14A duty about the contractor's expertise and measures` `a company that hired the agency in 2010`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 14A duty about the contractor's expertise and measures` `the security agency`
#ASSERT NOT `owes the section 12(1) duty to the person as its employee` `the security agency` `a visitor to the tower`

§ `21(2) -- who may be served with an order`

#ASSERT `may be served with a remedial or stop-work order` `the software company` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol`
#ASSERT `may be served with a remedial or stop-work order` `the security agency` `the leased office tower` `the wet stairwell` `the security officer on patrol`
